# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data and models - regenerate with `make seed`, never commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/generated/

# Model artifacts are the exception, and it is a decision rather than an
# oversight. An earlier rule here ignored `apps/scoring/models/*.joblib`;
# ADR-0010 section 6 supersedes it and commits registry entries to the
# repository, so that a demo can score without someone running a training job
# first — a demo that cannot be seen working is not a demo.
#
# The ceiling that makes it defensible is enforced by the training command
# (MAX_ARTIFACT_BYTES), not by this file: the measured artifact is 4 KB.
#
# The old rule would not have covered the entries anyway. `models/*.joblib` does
# not match `models/<name>/<version>/model.joblib`, because a single asterisk
# does not cross a directory separator — so the artifact was already being
# committed, by accident rather than by choice. Stated here so the next reader
# does not re-add it.

